# GitHub Linguist overrides.
#
# Linguist (https://github.com/github-linguist/linguist) drives the
# language-mix bar on github.com and the "Languages" sidebar. It
# counts bytes per file and attributes each to a detected language.
# These rules exclude vendored, generated, and build-glue files so
# the displayed mix reflects the project's own source — not the
# third-party ICU SDK we ship for build convenience or the data
# files compiled from CLDR.

# ── Vendored third-party C++ ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# `c_src/platform/osx/icu/unicode/` contains 200+ ICU header files
# (~5 MB) bundled so the NIF can be built without a system-wide ICU
# install. They are not part of the Localize source.
c_src/platform/**          linguist-vendored

# ── Build glue ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The NIF Makefile and its included env file are infrastructure,
# not project source.
c_src/Makefile             linguist-vendored
c_src/env.mk               linguist-vendored

# ── Generated CLDR data ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Erlang Term Format files compiled from upstream CLDR data. They
# ship with the package so consumers don't need a build-time CLDR
# pipeline, but they are not source code authored in this repo.
*.etf                      linguist-generated
priv/gettext/**.po         linguist-generated
priv/gettext/**.pot        linguist-generated

# ── Treat ETF as binary in diffs ─────────────────────────────────
*.etf                      binary
